    "lifecycle_state" : "DRAFTED",
    "details" : {
      "en" : {
        "id" : "en",
        "purpose" : "To assign FIGO 2009 stage for endometrial cancer from independently recorded anatomical, nodal, and distant-spread findings.",
        "keywords" : [
          "figo",
          "endometrial",
          "cancer",
          "uterine",
          "staging",
          "oncology",
          "gynecology",
          "tumor"
        ],
        "use" : "Use the separate findings in the endometrial observation to derive FIGO 2009 stage. Myometrial depth, cervical stromal invasion, serosal/adnexal involvement, vaginal/parametrial involvement, pelvic and para-aortic nodal status, bladder/rectal mucosal invasion, and distant metastasis are recorded independently. Negative findings must be distinguished from not assessed. Isolated tumour cells (N0(i+)) do not count as nodal metastasis for FIGO stage assignment. The guideline uses the highest applicable stage: IVB distant metastasis; IVA bladder/rectal mucosal invasion; IIIC2 para-aortic nodes; IIIC1 pelvic nodes; IIIB vagina/parametria; IIIA serosa/adnexa; II cervical stroma; IB ≥50% myometrial invasion; IA no invasion or <50%; I when confined to uterus but depth is not assessed. If required information is absent or not assessed, stage cannot be assigned.",
        "misuse" : "Not to be used to record the staging for other gynecological cancers.",
        "copyright" : "© Cambio CDS"
      }
    },
    "other_details" : {
      "en" : "An assessment tool used to assign the prognostic FIGO stage for endometrial cancer according to the FIGO 2009 staging system.",
      "references" : "Pecorelli S. Revised FIGO staging for carcinoma of the vulva, cervix, and endometrium. Int J Gynaecol Obstet. 2009 May;105(2):103-4. doi: 10.1016/j.ijgo.2009.02.012. Erratum in: Int J Gynaecol Obstet. 2010 Feb;108(2):176. PMID: 19367689.\n\nBerek JS, Matias-Guiu X, Creutzberg C, Fotopoulou C, Gaffney D, Kehoe S, Lindemann K, Mutch D, Concin N; Endometrial Cancer Staging Subcommittee, FIGO Women's Cancer Committee. FIGO staging of endometrial cancer: 2023. Int J Gynaecol Obstet. 2023 Aug;162(2):383-394. doi: 10.1002/ijgo.14923. Epub 2023 Jun 20. Erratum in: Int J Gynaecol Obstet. 2024 Sep;166(3):1374. doi: 10.1002/ijgo.15193. PMID: 37337978.\n\nMatsuo K, Klar M, Song BB, Roman LD, Wright JD. Validation of the 2023 FIGO staging schema for advanced endometrial cancer. Eur J Cancer. 2023 Nov;193:113316. doi: 10.1016/j.ejca.2023.113316. Epub 2023 Sep 21. PMID: 37741790.\n\nNationellt vårdprogram livmoderkroppscancer [Internet]. Regionala cancercentrum i samverkan; [cited 2026 Jul 10]. Available from: https://kunskapsbanken.cancercentrum.se/diagnoser/livmoderkroppscancer/vardprogram/kategorisering-av-tumoren/\nPecorelli S. Revised FIGO staging for carcinoma of the vulva, cervix, and endometrium. Int J Gynaecol Obstet. 2009;105(2):103-4."
    }
  },
